1
00:00:00,653 --> 00:00:03,142
Thank God, His people keep growing!

2
00:00:03,142 --> 00:00:06,373
Every Sunday, more families fill our churches,

3
00:00:06,373 --> 00:00:09,025
and more little feet come running through the doors.

4
00:00:09,653 --> 00:00:13,155
But here's the question every priest quietly asks.

5
00:00:13,155 --> 00:00:14,181
Who came today?

6
00:00:14,181 --> 00:00:14,900
Who didn't?

7
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:16,917
And who has been missing for weeks,

8
00:00:16,917 --> 00:00:18,450
without anyone noticing?

9
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:19,959
Paper lists get lost.

10
00:00:19,959 --> 00:00:21,245
Names get forgotten.

11
00:00:21,245 --> 00:00:23,933
And the people who need a phone call the most are the easiest

12
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:24,876
to miss.

13
00:00:25,493 --> 00:00:26,931
That's why we built Amoinee.

14
00:00:26,931 --> 00:00:30,233
It comes from the Coptic word for "Come!" It helps every

15
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:32,745
church know its people, care for them,

16
00:00:32,745 --> 00:00:34,254
and never lose one of them.

17
00:00:34,254 --> 00:00:36,659
So let's see how it works, step by step.

18
00:00:37,284 --> 00:00:39,030
It all starts with the members.

19
00:00:39,030 --> 00:00:41,235
Create your profile just once.

20
00:00:41,235 --> 00:00:43,912
Your name, your phone, your email,

21
00:00:43,912 --> 00:00:47,414
your address, and your church, which you simply start typing

22
00:00:47,414 --> 00:00:48,699
and pick from the list.

23
00:00:48,699 --> 00:00:51,222
It takes a minute, and it works on any phone.

24
00:00:51,854 --> 00:00:54,354
You also choose whether to turn on face check-in.

25
00:00:54,354 --> 00:00:57,833
Say yes, sign the consent, and take a quick face setup.

26
00:00:57,833 --> 00:01:00,074
Say no, and that's perfectly fine,

27
00:01:00,074 --> 00:01:01,878
because there are other ways to check in.

28
00:01:01,878 --> 00:01:04,284
And you can always take it back: turn it off,

29
00:01:04,284 --> 00:01:06,417
and your face data is deleted.

30
00:01:07,024 --> 00:01:10,421
If you choose face check-in, the setup takes under a minute.

31
00:01:10,421 --> 00:01:13,310
You look at the camera, then turn a little to the left,

32
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:14,454
then to the right.

33
00:01:14,454 --> 00:01:16,671
Three short captures, and that's it.

34
00:01:16,671 --> 00:01:19,218
Amoinee keeps only a numeric template,

35
00:01:19,218 --> 00:01:22,944
never a photo, and if the picture is too dark or blurry,

36
00:01:22,944 --> 00:01:24,796
it simply asks you to try again.

37
00:01:24,796 --> 00:01:27,024
You can withdraw your consent any time,

38
00:01:27,024 --> 00:01:29,264
and the data is erased on the spot.

39
00:01:29,894 --> 00:01:33,291
At the church door stands the Amoinee kiosk,

40
00:01:33,291 --> 00:01:35,743
a tablet on a stand that an admin signs in.

41
00:01:35,743 --> 00:01:38,444
Before the service, it just shows what's coming next,

42
00:01:38,444 --> 00:01:40,083
with the camera switched off.

43
00:01:40,083 --> 00:01:43,136
When check-in opens, it wakes up all by itself.

44
00:01:43,764 --> 00:01:46,453
The kiosk is only for church devices,

45
00:01:46,453 --> 00:01:48,257
so an admin has to be signed in.

46
00:01:48,257 --> 00:01:51,595
To leave it, press and hold the logo for two seconds,

47
00:01:51,595 --> 00:01:54,861
then type the admin password, so no one wanders out of it by

48
00:01:54,861 --> 00:01:55,780
accident.

49
00:01:56,414 --> 00:01:57,370
Now watch.

50
00:01:57,370 --> 00:01:59,563
Someone walks in, looks at the screen,

51
00:01:59,563 --> 00:02:01,851
and in a second it says, welcome, by name.

52
00:02:01,851 --> 00:02:03,348
It records that you're here.

53
00:02:03,348 --> 00:02:06,603
It even checks that it's a real face and not a photo.

54
00:02:06,603 --> 00:02:08,549
And it takes one person at a time,

55
00:02:08,549 --> 00:02:10,246
so everyone gets their moment.

56
00:02:10,884 --> 00:02:12,535
Prefer not to use your face?

57
00:02:12,535 --> 00:02:15,389
Just scan the QR code on the kiosk with your phone,

58
00:02:15,389 --> 00:02:16,356
and you're checked in.

59
00:02:16,356 --> 00:02:19,975
The code changes every minute, so it can't be passed around.

60
00:02:20,624 --> 00:02:23,655
Or type the three-digit code of the day in the app.

61
00:02:23,655 --> 00:02:27,134
Three simple ways to check in, and nobody is ever left at the

62
00:02:27,134 --> 00:02:27,923
door.

63
00:02:28,564 --> 00:02:30,982
And members can open My History at any time,

64
00:02:30,982 --> 00:02:32,975
to see every service they attended,

65
00:02:32,975 --> 00:02:34,448
with the date and time.

66
00:02:35,094 --> 00:02:37,748
Now let's see what Abouna and the servants get.

67
00:02:37,748 --> 00:02:40,329
This is where attendance turns into care.

68
00:02:40,954 --> 00:02:42,865
The Today screen is live.

69
00:02:42,865 --> 00:02:46,190
As people arrive, their names pop up with the arrival time,

70
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:49,516
whether they came by face, QR code or the daily code.

71
00:02:49,516 --> 00:02:51,768
You see who is on time and who is late,

72
00:02:51,768 --> 00:02:54,410
who is still missing, and you can check someone in by hand

73
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:55,576
with one tap.

74
00:02:56,226 --> 00:02:57,582
Someone forgot their phone?

75
00:02:57,582 --> 00:03:00,731
Under Not Here Yet, one tap checks them in by hand,

76
00:03:00,731 --> 00:03:02,570
and it's marked as added by an admin.

77
00:03:02,570 --> 00:03:04,351
You can also start a service yourself,

78
00:03:04,351 --> 00:03:07,924
choose the kind and the time, and end it when it's over.

79
00:03:07,924 --> 00:03:10,246
Everything is saved for the reports.

80
00:03:10,881 --> 00:03:12,909
Services open by themselves.

81
00:03:12,909 --> 00:03:16,329
Set your weekly events once, like the Divine Liturgy on

82
00:03:16,329 --> 00:03:19,784
Sunday morning, and check-in opens and closes on time.

83
00:03:19,784 --> 00:03:21,470
Each church has its own list of services,

84
00:03:21,470 --> 00:03:24,194
like Vespers, Bible Study, Sunday School,

85
00:03:24,194 --> 00:03:26,919
choir, youth, and family meetings.

86
00:03:26,919 --> 00:03:29,547
Add or remove your own, any time.

87
00:03:30,174 --> 00:03:32,981
The Members page keeps every person in one place,

88
00:03:32,981 --> 00:03:35,068
numbered and easy to search by name,

89
00:03:35,068 --> 00:03:37,439
phone, city or church.

90
00:03:37,439 --> 00:03:41,071
Filter by men, women, deacons, or visitors.

91
00:03:41,071 --> 00:03:45,387
Open any profile to add a photo, call or text with one tap,

92
00:03:45,387 --> 00:03:48,111
see their family, and write private notes that only your

93
00:03:48,111 --> 00:03:49,654
church's admins can read.

94
00:03:50,253 --> 00:03:52,576
Adding a member takes about a minute:

95
00:03:52,576 --> 00:03:56,326
name, gender, birthday, phone, email,

96
00:03:56,326 --> 00:03:58,755
address, city and church.

97
00:03:58,755 --> 00:04:02,505
If they agree, add face consent, and parents can sign for

98
00:04:02,505 --> 00:04:04,097
their children under eighteen.

99
00:04:04,097 --> 00:04:07,812
Open a profile for tabs on notes, attendance and consent,

100
00:04:07,812 --> 00:04:10,654
and make someone a deacon, or change their status,

101
00:04:10,654 --> 00:04:11,796
with one tap.

102
00:04:12,444 --> 00:04:16,171
And now, the heart of Amoinee: the Attendance Sheet.

103
00:04:16,171 --> 00:04:19,213
At the top, a short summary in plain words.

104
00:04:19,213 --> 00:04:22,043
How many people came, the average per service,

105
00:04:22,043 --> 00:04:23,859
and how many need a follow-up.

106
00:04:23,859 --> 00:04:26,171
Four big numbers show the average attendance,

107
00:04:26,171 --> 00:04:29,355
the attendance rate, how many attend every week,

108
00:04:29,355 --> 00:04:30,698
and how many need a call.

109
00:04:31,331 --> 00:04:32,840
Below, simple charts.

110
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,196
Who came at least once.

111
00:04:34,196 --> 00:04:37,427
Attendance over time, compared with the period before.

112
00:04:37,427 --> 00:04:40,576
How many attend every week, how many come often,

113
00:04:40,576 --> 00:04:42,439
sometimes, or rarely.

114
00:04:42,439 --> 00:04:43,795
What time people arrive.

115
00:04:43,795 --> 00:04:46,684
And men, women and deacons at each service.

116
00:04:47,326 --> 00:04:48,482
Then the register.

117
00:04:48,482 --> 00:04:52,373
One little square for every person at every service,

118
00:04:52,373 --> 00:04:55,180
like the paper register of old, but alive.

119
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:57,987
And the ranked list puts everyone in order,

120
00:04:57,987 --> 00:05:00,581
from the people who attend every single week,

121
00:05:00,581 --> 00:05:03,470
with a medal for the top three, to those who could use a

122
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:04,484
gentle call.

123
00:05:04,484 --> 00:05:07,031
You'll see streaks, the last visit,

124
00:05:07,031 --> 00:05:09,023
and how late they usually arrive.

125
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:12,768
Everything here can be filtered: any period,

126
00:05:12,768 --> 00:05:14,914
one kind of service, or one group,

127
00:05:14,914 --> 00:05:17,048
like the deacons or a family.

128
00:05:17,048 --> 00:05:20,150
Each chart has a table view, and tapping a group like Absent

129
00:05:20,150 --> 00:05:22,131
shows exactly who is in it.

130
00:05:22,131 --> 00:05:24,796
And one tap switches between the dark look and the parchment

131
00:05:24,796 --> 00:05:25,455
look.

132
00:05:34,254 --> 00:05:36,483
When someone misses a few Sundays,

133
00:05:36,483 --> 00:05:39,667
Amoinee gently marks them "Follow up needed",

134
00:05:39,667 --> 00:05:41,577
so nobody slips through the cracks.

135
00:05:41,577 --> 00:05:43,264
Then your servants can add labels:

136
00:05:43,264 --> 00:05:46,625
Called, Visited, Needs prayer, Traveling,

137
00:05:46,625 --> 00:05:48,594
Sick, Away at college.

138
00:05:48,594 --> 00:05:51,542
They can snooze a reminder when it's not the right time,

139
00:05:51,542 --> 00:05:54,100
and everyone sees who is taking care of whom.

140
00:05:54,724 --> 00:05:57,154
And when that person comes back, they show up under Welcome

141
00:05:57,154 --> 00:05:59,158
Back, so you can greet them warmly.

142
00:05:59,158 --> 00:06:03,415
You'll also see who is new, and whose birthday is this week,

143
00:06:03,415 --> 00:06:05,313
so every member feels remembered.

144
00:06:05,954 --> 00:06:07,865
You're not limited to our labels.

145
00:06:07,865 --> 00:06:10,011
In Manage Labels, create your own,

146
00:06:10,011 --> 00:06:11,827
with a name in English and Arabic,

147
00:06:11,827 --> 00:06:13,737
an emoji, and a color.

148
00:06:13,737 --> 00:06:16,957
Tick this box for labels like Traveling or Sick,

149
00:06:16,957 --> 00:06:19,952
and Amoinee stops asking you to follow up while they are

150
00:06:19,952 --> 00:06:20,813
active.

151
00:06:20,813 --> 00:06:24,233
Reorder them or turn them off, and every change is kept in

152
00:06:24,233 --> 00:06:25,175
the history.

153
00:06:25,824 --> 00:06:29,103
Because behind every name is a person who may be waiting for

154
00:06:29,103 --> 00:06:29,857
a call.

155
00:06:29,857 --> 00:06:33,289
A word of encouragement, a visit, a prayer,

156
00:06:33,289 --> 00:06:34,680
can bring someone home.

157
00:06:35,281 --> 00:06:36,212
Need a report?

158
00:06:36,212 --> 00:06:40,281
With one tap, Abouna gets a one-page summary to print or save

159
00:06:40,281 --> 00:06:43,441
as a PDF, in English or in Arabic.

160
00:06:43,441 --> 00:06:46,944
And the full data goes to Excel, with the register,

161
00:06:46,944 --> 00:06:49,490
the follow-up list, and the label history.

162
00:06:50,146 --> 00:06:52,269
Here is that one-page report.

163
00:06:52,269 --> 00:06:55,099
The church, the period, a plain summary,

164
00:06:55,099 --> 00:06:57,752
the big numbers, the charts, the top attenders,

165
00:06:57,752 --> 00:06:59,179
and the follow-up list.

166
00:06:59,179 --> 00:07:01,325
It's perfect for a meeting with the servants,

167
00:07:01,325 --> 00:07:02,941
or to keep in your archive.

168
00:07:02,941 --> 00:07:06,277
Choose the English or the Arabic version before you print.

169
00:07:06,914 --> 00:07:08,943
Access is simple and safe.

170
00:07:08,943 --> 00:07:11,926
Anyone can ask to become an admin of their church,

171
00:07:11,926 --> 00:07:13,895
and an existing admin approves it.

172
00:07:13,895 --> 00:07:16,655
Each admin sees only their own church,

173
00:07:16,655 --> 00:07:19,708
and the super admin can switch between churches.

174
00:07:20,343 --> 00:07:23,869
A priest or servant who wants access opens My Profile,

175
00:07:23,869 --> 00:07:27,418
chooses their church, and taps Request admin access.

176
00:07:27,418 --> 00:07:29,010
The admin sees it under Approvals,

177
00:07:29,010 --> 00:07:32,194
with a red badge, and approves or declines it.

178
00:07:32,194 --> 00:07:34,682
You can also invite someone by email before they even have an

179
00:07:34,682 --> 00:07:38,232
account, and they become an admin the first time they sign

180
00:07:38,232 --> 00:07:38,810
up.

181
00:07:38,810 --> 00:07:40,590
So there are three kinds of people:

182
00:07:40,590 --> 00:07:43,703
members, who need no approval; church admins,

183
00:07:43,703 --> 00:07:46,817
who manage one church; and one super admin,

184
00:07:46,817 --> 00:07:49,056
who can switch between all churches.

185
00:07:49,704 --> 00:07:51,792
Your people's trust matters most.

186
00:07:51,792 --> 00:07:55,294
Face data is only a number, never a photo,

187
00:07:55,294 --> 00:07:56,839
and only with consent.

188
00:07:56,839 --> 00:08:00,388
Notes and labels are visible to admins of that church alone,

189
00:08:00,388 --> 00:08:02,688
never to members, and never on the kiosk.

190
00:08:02,688 --> 00:08:06,509
Every change is logged, and each church only ever sees its

191
00:08:06,509 --> 00:08:07,510
own people.

192
00:08:08,164 --> 00:08:11,773
Because every soul matters, and no one should be forgotten.

193
00:08:11,773 --> 00:08:12,669
Amoinee.

194
00:08:12,669 --> 00:08:14,107
Come, let us worship.

